WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:08.775
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]
&gt;&gt; IT'S THE MAN WITH THE CLOTH.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.411
&gt;&gt; I CAN'T BELIEVE SCAREY STORES
STILL WORK ON ME.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; WHAT ABOUT YOU, BRANDON, DO
YOU HAVE ANY GOOD ONES?

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; MAYBE WE SHOULD TURN IN.
&gt;&gt; COME ON, MAN.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:24.290
&gt;&gt; IT WOULD BE NICE TO HEAR A
STORY IF YOU HAVE ONE, BRANDON.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; FINE.
YOU WANT TO BE SCARED?

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.729
I HAVE A STORY.
ONLY THING IS IT'S NOT A STORY.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
IT'S REAL.
IT HAPPENED TO ME ABOUT TWO

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:36.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
YEARS AGO WHEN I WAS STILL AT
THE AD AGENCY.

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I GOT A CALL FROM MY DAD.
&gt;&gt; WHAT DID HE SAY?

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:44.944
&gt;&gt; HE ASKED ME IF I COULD GET A
COFFEE WITH HIS FRIEND'S SON.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:49.616
&gt;&gt; THAT'S NO BIG DEAL, RIGHT?
&gt;&gt; A 22-YEAR-OLD RECENT COLLEGE

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
GRAD.
AND AN EXPIRING FILMMAKER.

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:57.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; SO DID YOU DO IT?
YEP.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
HIS NAME WAS CONOR.
AND HE HAD A LOT TO SAY.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:03.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; WHAT'S AT THE MOVIES THESE
DAYS?

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.801
EVERYTHING IS A REBOOT.
HOLLYWOOD HAS NO ORIGINAL IDEAS.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:12.972
IT'S ALWAYS GUY MEETS GIRL.
THAT'S WHY WHEN I MAKE MY MOVIES

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:16.843
THINGS WILL BE DIFFERENT, TRUST
ME.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; RIGHT.
&gt;&gt; SO HIS TAKE WAS THAT BASIC?

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.514
&gt;&gt; EXACTLY.
BUT LIKE HE WAS THE FIRST PERSON

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
WHO EVER SAID IT.
&gt;&gt; HOW LONG WERE YOU THERE?

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:29.456
&gt;&gt; TWO AND A HALF HOURS.
LITERALLY TO BREAK DOWN THE

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:32.692
STATE OF THE INDUSTRY.
&gt;&gt; CGI WHEN IS EVERYTHING BASED

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:36.896
ON VIDEO GAME OR ROLLER COASTER.
HELLO "ACCESS HOLLYWOOD" CAN YOU

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
MAKE SOMETHING ABOUT REAL
PAPERS.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:43.770
THAT'S WHY I WOULD SAY A WARNING
THIS MOVIE MIGHT MAKE YOU THINK.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.107
I REALLY LIKE TALKING TO YOU.
&gt;&gt; HOLD ON THIS IS CRAZY, HE HAD

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:50.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
A BACK UP PLAN.
&gt;&gt; NO, JUST FILM.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; DID HE HAVE ANY IDEAS?
LIKE DID HE TELL YOU WHAT HIS

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:58.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
MOVIES WOULD BE ABOUT?
&gt;&gt; OH, YEAH, HE HAD AN IDEA.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.287
&gt;&gt; DUDE, THIS SHOULD BE A MOVIE.
JUST LIKE YOU AND ME TALKING

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
ABOUT MOVIES.
THAT'S WHAT REAL LIFE IS.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; THEN YOU LEFT, RIGHT?
&gt;&gt; I TRIED.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:14.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; BUT THAT'S WHEN HE SAID IT.
&gt;&gt; HEY, COOL IF I GET YOUR

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
NUMBER?
&gt;&gt; STOP.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; DID HE EVER CALL YOU?
&gt;&gt; NO.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:20.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
NO, NO, NO.
HE TEXTED.

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:26.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
3D, DUDE, HURTS MY EYES.
SO EXPENSIVE.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
THAT FEELS LIKE TV IS THE NEW
MOVIES.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
HAPPY THANKSGIVING BROTHER.
&gt;&gt; THERE ARE SO MANY.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.885
&gt;&gt; BUT HE HAS TO LEAVE YOU ALONE
EVENTUALLY.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:35.054
HE CAN'T TEXT YOU AND PICK YOUR
BRAIN FOREVER?

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:40.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; NO, HE STAYS WITH ME.
UNLESS I CAN INTRODUCE HIM TO

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:45.832
SOMEONE ELSE HE CAN TALK TO.
THAT'S HOW THE CURSE WORKS.

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:48.268
&gt;&gt; YOU ARE NOT GOING TO DO THAT,
RIGHT?

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:51.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; I'M SO SORRY.
&gt;&gt; NO.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; HEY, MAN, ERIC, REMEMBER MY
PODCAST?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.143
WE TALK ABOUT CLASSIC HOLLYWOOD
FILM.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
&gt;&gt; NO!

